License composition
-------------------

The VS-05 fork contains code under several licenses. Per the fork policy,
**new code added by this project is GPL-3.0-or-later**, while all other code
keeps whatever license it already declares. In particular:

| Component | License |
|---|---|
| New code added by the VS-05 fork | **GPL-3.0-or-later** |
| Original 2013-era engine code | **GPL-2.0-or-later** (`LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt`) |
| Dear ImGui (vendored, `libraries/imgui/`) | **MIT** (`LICENSES/MIT.txt`) |
| imstb_* single-file libraries (in imgui) | **Public domain** (`LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt`) |
| `objconv/blender_xmesh_import.txt` | GPL (Alex Feterman) |

The GPL-2.0-or-later engine code is compatible with GPL-3.0-or-later by virtue
of its "or (at your option) any later version" clause, so the combined work is
licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later.

Individual source files carry SPDX license identifiers in their headers where
practical. The `LICENSES/` directory holds the full text of each license used.
